From 4fcd38b4c2168983d68c248b62360bf4a8b6cb09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:55:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tests: FakeService release refuses non-object extra,
 counts numbers like JSON.stringify, refuses spawn_failed on ops

PR #1999 review nits (pullrequestreview-5888197293), compared against
hermes-hub worker/src/transitions.ts releaseTask / releaseDiagnostic:

1. releaseTask refuses `op.extra ?? {}` that is not an object as `invalid`
   ("failure extra must be an object") right before releaseDiagnostic. The
   fake read `op.get("extra") or {}`, so [], "", 0 and False silently became
   {}. New FakeService.release_inputs does the extra check then
   release_diagnostic; both the ops route (release_op) and the leases route
   use it, so a non-object extra is `invalid` and changes nothing.
2. release_diagnostic measured json.dumps, which writes 1.0 as "1.0", 1e-7
   as "1e-07" and NaN/Infinity as NaN/Infinity; JSON.stringify writes "1",
   "1e-7" and null. _js_stringify/_js_number reproduce Number::toString from
   the shortest round-trip digits, so the 8000-char boundary matches for
   numbers too (lone surrogates stay out of scope, as documented).
3. release_op accepted spawn_failed and only ended the run with a
   spawn_failed event, while the leases route raises NotImplementedError
   (the real releaseTask goes through endCustody + recordTaskFailure).
   release_op now raises the same NotImplementedError before any write.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_rejections.py): 72 non-object-extra
cases x routes, 21 number-length cases, spawn_failed on both routes; 87 of
them fail on the pre-change fake, all 230 in the file pass after.
